From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Thu, 04 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chelper: disable runtime build check

Embedded target has no gcc; chelper is pre-compiled by the cross
toolchain at Buildroot build time (see KLIPPER_BUILD_CMDS in
klipper.mk).  Comment out the runtime mtime-based rebuild attempt so
klippy never tries to invoke gcc on the target.

Empirically the happy path (KLIPPER_INSTALL_TARGET_CMDS: cp -r the
source tree, then INSTALL c_helper.so last) already leaves the .so
strictly newer than every source file, so check_build_code returns
False and no gcc invocation occurs.  This patch is a defensive guard
against future post-install hooks, OTA scripts, or `find -exec touch`
flows that could re-touch a chelper source AFTER the .so install,
which WOULD trigger a rebuild attempt (verified by adversarial test,
2026-06-04).

Identical change is present in github.com/FlashForge/AD5M_Series_Klipper
(see docs/research/2026-06-04-klipper-v0.11-fork-deltas.md §2.1).

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/chelper/__init__.py | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/klippy/chelper/__init__.py b/klippy/chelper/__init__.py
--- a/klippy/chelper/__init__.py
+++ b/klippy/chelper/__init__.py
@@ -266,13 +266,15 @@ def get_ffi():
         srcfiles = get_abs_files(srcdir, SOURCE_FILES)
         ofiles = get_abs_files(srcdir, OTHER_FILES)
         destlib = get_abs_files(srcdir, [DEST_LIB])[0]
-        if check_build_code(srcfiles+ofiles+[__file__], destlib):
-            if check_gcc_option(SSE_FLAGS):
-                cmd = "%s %s %s" % (GCC_CMD, SSE_FLAGS, COMPILE_ARGS)
-            else:
-                cmd = "%s %s" % (GCC_CMD, COMPILE_ARGS)
-            logging.info("Building C code module %s", DEST_LIB)
-            do_build_code(cmd % (destlib, ' '.join(srcfiles)))
+        # ReForge: pre-compiled by cross toolchain at Buildroot time; skip the
+        # runtime mtime-based rebuild (no gcc on target).  See klipper.mk.
+        # if check_build_code(srcfiles+ofiles+[__file__], destlib):
+        #     if check_gcc_option(SSE_FLAGS):
+        #         cmd = "%s %s %s" % (GCC_CMD, SSE_FLAGS, COMPILE_ARGS)
+        #     else:
+        #         cmd = "%s %s" % (GCC_CMD, COMPILE_ARGS)
+        #     logging.info("Building C code module %s", DEST_LIB)
+        #     do_build_code(cmd % (destlib, ' '.join(srcfiles)))
         FFI_main = cffi.FFI()
         for d in defs_all:
             FFI_main.cdef(d)
